uccessful effort to bring back the ten tribes to their allegiance.","verses":20,"father":"Rehoboam","mother":"Maachah","v":[1,2,3,4,15,17,19,20,21,22]},{"id":"maachah_1841","name":"Maachah","also":"Michaiah","summary":"The daughter of Abishalom (called Absalom, 2 Chr. 11:20-22), the third wife of Rehoboam, and mother of Abijam (1 Kings 15:2). She is called “Michaiah the daughter of Uriel,” who was the husband of Absalom’s daughter Tamar (2 Chr. 13:2).","verses":8,"father":"Uriel","mother":"Tamar","v":[2]},{"id":"uriel_2902","name":"Uriel","also":"","summary":"The father of Michaiah, one of Rehoboam’s wives, and mother of Abijah (2 Chr. 13:2).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[2]},{"id":"ephraim_1206","name":"Ephraim","also":"","summary":"Double fruitfulness (“for God had made him fruitful in the land of his affliction”). The second son of Joseph, born in Egypt (Gen. 41:52; 46:20).","verses":160,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[4]},{"id":"david_994","name":"David","also":"","summary":"Beloved, the eighth and youngest son of Jesse, a citizen of Bethlehem. His father seems to have been a man in humble life. His mother’s name is not recorded.","verses":896,"father":"Jesse","mother":"","v":[5,6,8]},{"id":"solomon_2762","name":"Solomon","also":"Jedidiah","summary":"Peaceful, (Heb. Shelomoh), David’s second son by Bathsheba, i.e., the first after their legal marriage (2 Sam. 12). He was probably born about B.C. 1035 (1 Chr. 22:5; 29:1).","verses":273,"father":"David","mother":"Bathsheba","v":[6,7]},{"id":"nebat_2165","name":"Nebat","also":"","summary":"Sight; aspect, the father of Jeroboam, the king of Israel (1 Kings 11:26, etc.).","verses":25,"father":"","mother":"","v":[6]},{"id":"rehoboam_2412","name":"Rehoboam","also":"Roboam","summary":"He enlarges the people, the successor of Solomon on the throne, and apparently his only son. He was the son of Naamah “the Ammonitess,” some well-known Ammonitish princess (1 Kings 14:21; 2 Chr. 12:13).","verses":42,"father":"Solomon","mother":"Naamah","v":[7]},{"id":"aaron_1","name":"Aaron","also":"","summary":"The eldest son of Amram and Jochebed, a daughter of Levi (Ex. 6:20). Some explain the name as meaning mountaineer, others mountain of strength, illuminator.","verses":331,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[9,10]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[12,16,18]},{"id":"iddo_1594","name":"Iddo","also":"","summary":"Lovely. A prophet of Judah who wrote the history of Rehoboam and Abijah (2 Chr. 12:15).","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[22]}],"places":[{"id":"gibeah_467","name":"Gibeah","kind":"","lat":31.43333,"lon":35.13333,"summary":"(Josh. 15:57, R.V. marg.), a city on Mount Ephraim which had been given to Phinehas (24:33 “hill,” A.V.; R.V. marg. and Heb., “Gibeah.”). Here Eleazar the son of Aaron was buried.","verses":2,"v":[2]},{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[2]},{"id":"mount_zemaraim_859","name":"mount Zemaraim","kind":"Mountain","lat":31.911,"lon":35.45728,"summary":"A mount in the highlands of Ephraim, to the north of Jerusalem (2 Chr. 13:4-20).","verses":1,"v":[4]},{"id":"bethel_202","name":"Bethel","kind":"","lat":31.93054,"lon":35.22103,"summary":"A place in Central Palestine, about 10 miles north of Jerusalem, at the head of the pass of Michmash and Ai. It was originally the royal Canaanite city of Luz (Gen. 28:19).","verses":62,"v":[19]},{"id":"ephron_406","name":"Ephron","kind":"Settlement","lat":31.95379,"lon":35.29914,"summary":"","verses":1,"v":[19]},{"id":"jeshanah_638","name":"Jeshanah","kind":"City","lat":31.98003,"lon":35.22971,"summary":"A city of the kingdom of Israel (2 Chr. 13:19).","verses":1,"v":[19]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[8083,8083,8083,8141,3379,3379,4428,29,4427,4427,5921,3063],[4427,4427,4427,3389,3389,7969,8141,517,517,8034,4322,4322,1323,222,222,4480,4480,4480,1390,1961,1961,1961,4421,996,29,3379,3379],[29,631,4421,4421,2428,2428,2428,702,702,977,376,3379,3379,6186,6186,4421,4421,5973,5973,8083,8083,977,1368,1368,376,2428,2428],[29,29,6965,5921,2022,6787,2022,2022,2022,2022,669,669,559,559,8085,8085,3379,3379,3605,3605,3478],[3808,3808,3808,3045,3588,3068,3068,430,430,3478,3478,5414,5414,4467,4467,5921,3478,1732,1732,1121,1121,1121,5769,1285,1285,1285,4417,4417],[3379,3379,1121,5028,5028,5650,5650,8010,8010,1121,1732,1732,6965,6965,4775,4775,5921,113,113],[7386,7386,1100,1100,1121,6908,5921,5921,553,553,7346,1121,8010,8010,7346,7346,1961,5288,7390,3808,3808,2388,2388,6440],[6258,6258,859,559,2388,2388,2388,4467,4467,3068,3068,3068,3027,3027,3027,3027,3027,1732,1732,1121,859,7227,7227,7227,7227,1995,5973,5973,5973,5973,5973,2091,2091,5695,834,3379,6213,0,0,430,430],[3808,3808,3808,3808,5080,5080,3548,3548,3068,3068,3068,1121,1121,175,175,3881,3881,3881,6213,6213,6213,6213,6213,3548,0,0,5971,5971,5971,5971,776,776,776,3605,3605,935,4390,4390,3027,6499,6499,6499,6499,7651,7651,352,1961,1961,3548,3548,3808,3808,3808,3808,3808,430],[587,587,587,587,3068,3068,430,430,430,3808,3808,3808,5800,5800,3548,3548,8334,8334,3068,3068,3068,1121,1121,175,175,3881,3881,3881,4399,4399,4399,4399],[1242,1242,6153,6153,6153,6999,6999,5930,5930,5561,5561,7004,3068,3068,3068,4635,4635,4635,4635,4635,3899,3899,5921,2889,2889,2889,7979,6153,6153,6153,1197,1197,5216,5216,2091,2091,2091,4501,587,8104,8104,8104,4931,4931,3068,3068,3068,430,430,859,859,5800,5800,853],[2009,2009,430,430,430,5973,5973,7218,